<title>NEW ZEALAND: RBNZ table of inflation forecasts.</title>
<headline>RBNZ table of inflation forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand in its six monthly economic projections statement on Thursday released the following table of its inflation forecasts (with previous forecasts from its six monthly monetary policy statement released in December, in brackets):</p>
<p>			   Underlying		     Headline</p>
<p>			  Qtrly	 Ann	    Qtrly	 Ann</p>
<p>Mar 1997	   0.5 (0.4)   2.2 (2.0)     0.1 (0.3)  2.2 (2.1)</p>
<p>June		 0.5 (0.2)   2.0 (1.4)     0.5 (0.2)  1.9 (1.5)</p>
<p>Sept		 0.3 (0.1)   1.9 (1.2)     0.3 (0.1)  1.6 (1.0)</p>
<p>Dec		  0.2 (0.1)   1.5 (0.8)     0.2 (0.1)  1.0 (0.6)</p>
<p>Mar 1998	   0.2 (0.1)   1.2 (0.5)     0.2 (0.1)  1.1 (0.5)</p>
<p>June		 0.2 (0.1)   0.8 (0.4)     0.1 (0.1)  0.7 (0.3)</p>
<p>Sept		 0.2 (0.1)   0.8 (0.4)     0.3 (0.1)  0.7 (0.3)</p>
<p>Dec		  0.3 (0.0)   0.8 (0.3)     0.3 (0.0)  0.8 (0.1)</p>
<p>Mar 1999	   0.4 (0.0)   1.1 (0.2)     0.4 (0.0)  1.0 (0.1)</p>
<p>Jun		  0.4	   1.3	     0.4	  1.3</p>
<p>Sept		 0.5	   1.6	     0.4	  1.5</p>
<p>Dec		  0.5	   1.8	     0.4	  1.6</p>
<p>March 2000	 0.6	   2.0	     0.5	  1.8</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4 4734746)</p>
</text>
